body: "## Problem\nStorage carries a format_version field and migration primitives are planned, but no test answers the practical questions: what does today's build do with a workspace written by last month's build, what does last month's build do with today's, and what happens when two such agents merge branches.\n\n## Approach\nA matrix job that installs prior published releases, generates representative workspaces with them, then runs the current build's read, mutate, validate, merge, and history-verify paths against those workspaces — and the mirror direction using the current build as writer.\n\n## Field preservation\nThe critical invariant is that an older reader must not destroy fields it does not understand. Round-trip preservation of unknown fields is what makes a staggered fleet safe, and it must be asserted explicitly.\n\n## Boundary\nNot schema migration itself, which is owned separately. This proves the compatibility window; migrations move workspaces across it."
